c) **Commercial Use**: The right to use the Work for commercial purposes, including but not limited to selling products or services that incorporate the Work.

### 3. Viral Copyleft Condition

This is the core condition of the Hyphen License 1.0:

a) **Fork Requirement**: Any work that is forked from a repository or codebase licensed under HLv1.0 must also be licensed entirely under HLv1.0.

b) **Derivative Works**: Any Derivative Work must be licensed as a whole at no charge to all third parties under the terms of this License. No additional restrictions may be imposed on recipients' exercise of the rights granted herein.

c) **Distribution Requirement**: When you Distribute any Work or Derivative Work, you must:
   - Include a copy of this License
   - Keep intact all notices referring to this License
   - Make the complete Source Code of the Derivative Work available under HLv1.0
   - Clearly indicate that the work is licensed under HLv1.0

d) **No Sublicensing**: You may not sublicense the Work under different terms. All distributions must remain under HLv1.0.

### 4. Source Code Availability

If you Distribute Object Code of the Work or any Derivative Work, you must also make the corresponding Source Code available under HLv1.0. The Source Code must be provided in a manner that allows recipients to modify and rebuild the Work.

